{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/987570-running-the-technocracy","id":987570,"title":"Running the Technocracy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-14T20:06:56-07:00","id":987570,"title":"Running the Technocracy","content":"How do you run a Technocratic Symposium? I re-read the section on Conclaves in Vampire, on the off-chance it would help. Also, I'm not sure what multi-Convention Horizon Constructs are like. Autochthonia's description sort of helps, as does Restricted Sectors from Digital Web 2.0.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T22:09:27-07:00","id":987612,"title":"","content":"Well, given that the Void Engineers see the titular Void as being space, I would imagine that a Horizon Construct would look like a space station or planetside base. From there, it's looking at examples of such things in media, and choosing what you want the place to look like, both inside and out. Such places certainly have gravity, and may or may not be operating under space limitations (as in, they may or may not need to have all the halls and rooms small and cramped). Which Convention holds the most sway in the Construct also matters. A Syndicate controlled one might be very posh (think Star Trek), while a Progenitor one would have plenty of sterile labs and controlled growing environments. Very large Constructs that cater to all Conventions might be full on <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arcology\" target=\"_blank\">Arcologies</a>, or attempts at &quot;terraforming&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T02:56:43-07:00","id":987686,"title":"","content":"For Symposiums, it can depend on the size. If it's a small one within a single construct then it's probably going to take the form of whichever convention is &quot;in charge&quot; with the other members fitting the form.<br /> <br /> I imagine this being as:<br /> <br /> Iteration X: Tech meeting style<br /> Progenitors: Lecture Theatre style<br /> Syndicate: Board room style<br /> NWO: Government/Agent debriefing style<br /> Void Engineers: Military style<br /> <br /> This, of course, will mostly depend on the intent of the meeting.<br /> <br /> For larger regional or international conventions, it depends on what the intent of the convention is. If it's a showcase of new technology then it will be more like a &quot;World Fair&quot; or &quot;expo&quot; setting with large amounts of space filled with various different groups showcasing new technology, new prototypes, and even new theories. Poster presentations and specialist lectures will be heald throughout the day. This is also a chance for scientists to showcase their preliminary work to potential investors and funding bodies as well as pitch ideas to a larger audience.<br /> <br /> The day will be bookended by grand meetings in a huge room where evryone is welcomed and encouraged to intermingle. At the end of the day there may be certain announcements made. If there is a competition to receive funding, for example, the winners will be announced.<br /> <br /> This style can work for business venture and college research aswell.<br /> <br /> <br /> If the convention is more for serious discussion and debate, as well as allocating teams towards specific investigations. These will be less lighthearted, especially if there's a pressing issue such as the Rogue Council all those years ago.<br /> At these events, amalgams and methodologies will gather and information will be discussed, debated, and reviewed. Plans of action suggested and procedures discussed.<br /> <br /> These events can become very political depending on the topic at hand, and may have a greater turnout of one specific convention or methodology. For example, a Convention specifically about the global financial market will have a greater turnout of Syndicate members, while one about Nephandi spawned epidemics will have more Progenitors.<br /> <br /> Conversely there may be conventions which only a small group of leaders attend, heads from various departments, in order to, for example, discuss the timetable and how the following year will work towards it's needs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T10:20:34-07:00","id":987811,"title":"","content":"As Saikou points out, the question might be too open.<br /> <br /> Who is running the Symposium? Why are they having it? Who is invited? Where is it?<br /> <br /> A lot of Symposia could be run in the mundane world in plain sight at a convention center near you. Some might take place on cramped space stations. (Or maybe not depending on where your Union is vis-a-vis the Discontinuity Event). You could have the whole thing go virtual and occur in a secured Sector on the Digital Web. If you want to go full on 1st Edition feel, you have it occur at an office building surrounded by the eternal static of an old-fashioned TV tuned to no station with the underlying hum of pure white noise.<br /> <br /> It could be a droning lecture. It could be the absolute epitome of a high school science fair with each Amalgam demoing it's latest best offering (in which case it could look like a cross with a lawn and garden show). Or a corporate retreat. Etc. etc.<br /> <br /> It all depends on what you have in mind. It's probably not done with all the archaic pomp and circumstance of a vampire Conclave or even what you would see in most intra- or inter-Traditions meetings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T10:19:13-07:00","id":990475,"title":"","content":"Yes, a symposium within the context of the technocracy is meant to revolve around a particular issue. For example an on going investigation against a reality deviant. However a symposium can also be an informal affair, like a party. Strange as it may sound the Technocracy are human beings and sometimes they too want to party, within the acceptable guidelines of proper technocrat behavior that is.<br /> <br /> I suppose the question is, what is the context of a this symposium and how would fit into your game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12570-anathema_dreamer","name":"Anathema_Dreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12570_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T19:14:15-07:00","id":991216,"title":"","content":"An interesting symposium would be one that would figure out the Enlightened Science behind a 'supernatural' phenomena, such as the Garou. With sufficient study, the Technocrats may figure out how to mimic the 'Gaia Signal' that permanently transforms Kinfolk into Garou. Of course, then the question would be what to do with it? Imagine if they decided that they would broadcast it onto a city like NYC as an experiment, where there might be 6,000 adult Kinfolk. Can you imagine the chaos that would occur if 6,000 Kinfolk transformed into Garou and experienced the First Change at the same time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T20:10:39-07:00","id":991234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> 